\name{sc_start}
\alias{sc_start}
\title{Start or reopen a reviewed analysis in the local browser}
\usage{
sc_start(input = NULL, project_dir, context = NULL, checkout = NULL,
  python = NULL, browse = interactive(), reuse_processed = FALSE,
  processed_reason = NULL, cluster_column = "seurat_clusters",
  model_suggestions = c("auto", "off", "configured", "simulate"),
  sample_id = NULL, matrix_kind = NULL, cell_metadata = NULL,
  feature_key = c("name", "id"), scientific_review = NULL,
  provider = NULL, review = list(allow_external = FALSE),
  doublet = c("auto", "off", "flag", "remove"),
  react = c("auto", "all", "off"), biological_diagnostics = TRUE,
  model_timeout = NULL, subcluster_workspace = NULL, reference_tissue = NULL)
}
\arguments{
\item{subcluster_workspace}{Separate existing nonsymlink directory for independent child analyses. NULL disables the workspace. Enabling it freezes completed parent review and exposes registered child Review and Cell scope routes; no child is created automatically.}
\item{reference_tissue}{Explicit exact ACT tissue key, separate from the unchanged study context tissue. NULL uses study tissue. Use annot_act_scopes(species) to inspect available keys. Creation only; changing reference evidence in an existing project uses sc_run_set_reference.}
\item{model_timeout}{Whole workbench suggestion-worker limit, integer seconds from 1 to 86400. NULL derives a conservative bound from baseline provider timeout, startup allowance and saved ReAct step/cluster limits, capped at 24 hours. Includes baseline and all ReAct clusters. This operator setting does not change saved scientific policy or provider timeouts. The launcher identity binds this operator setting, so a service with a different timeout is not reused.}
\item{react}{Annotation evidence checks: auto for difficult clusters (default), all, or off; alternatively a list accepted by the ReAct policy validator (for example mode, max_steps, max_steps_per_cluster, cluster_timeout_seconds, tool_timeout_seconds, max_payload_bytes). The byte setting also applies to one-shot requests; default unlimited disables the application byte quota, not model context limits. An optional finite quota accepts 1 to 1000000 bytes; scan projections use remaining request space. Saved settings are immutable on reopening.}
\item{biological_diagnostics}{Diagnostic-only coarse clusters and batch evidence for raw entry, TRUE by default. FALSE disables both; a list may independently disable cluster_qc or batch_assessment. Processed reuse defaults to disabled.}
\item{scientific_review}{Explicit optional rebuilding/extended expression diagnostics for a new raw project, disabled by default. Applicable declared-human blood/PBMC or pancreas classic panels remain baseline evidence. Reopening cannot replace saved settings.}
\item{input}{Local RDS file containing raw counts or a Seurat object, a 10x MEX directory, or a sample table data.frame/CSV/TSV. NULL reopens an existing project from protected checkpoints without rereading original inputs.}
\item{sample_id,matrix_kind}{For one 10x MEX directory, explicit sample ID and raw/filtered declaration. Sample tables instead require sample_id, path, matrix_kind columns. Optional donor/condition/batch/capture/treatment/qc_group/group columns declare those metadata roles. Filtered is a user declaration, not independent evidence of empty-droplet processing.}
\item{cell_metadata}{Optional data.frame/CSV/TSV keyed by sample_id and barcode. Must cover every imported barcode exactly once; joins use keys rather than row positions. Extra/missing/duplicate keys and overlapping sample/cell fields are rejected.}
\item{feature_key}{Original feature name (default) or compatible ID as analysis row names. ID/name/type and analysis keys are retained in assay metadata. Name mode gives incompatible names neutral technical keys and all duplicate-name members a stable feature-ID hash suffix; the local preapproval import summary lists the exact changes. No gene rows are collapsed. ID keys that Seurat would rename are rejected. ID keys may make symbol-based mitochondrial, cycle and reference evidence unavailable; no mapping is inferred. Across samples, require the same Gene Expression ID set and consistent annotations, then reorder by ID. Other modalities are excluded with counts recorded; no gene intersection/union is applied.}
\item{project_dir}{New project path or the same saved project to reopen.}
\item{context}{Declared species, tissue, research_goal and optional notes, columns and design; required for a new project, otherwise saved context is used.}
\item{checkout}{Optional matching developer checkout, selected explicitly or via options(scAgentKit.checkout=...). Installed package resources are the default.}
\item{model_suggestions}{Operator mode: auto (default; selects configured suggestions or mock simulation from the saved provider), off, configured, or simulate (immutable mock provider only). Preview and exact transfer authorization remain separate from scientific approval.}
\item{doublet}{Auto (default) or flag attempts eligible called-cell diagnostics and keeps cells; off explicitly leaves them unassessed. Remove stages an exact predicted-cell removal proposal only when prerequisites pass; human scientific approval remains required. Missing dependencies, capture or calling provenance are explicitly unassessed.}
\item{provider}{Explicit name/list, including name='openai_compatible' with HTTPS base_url, model and api_key_env. NULL detects exactly one DeepSeek/Grok key; missing or ambiguous keys fall back to manual mode with a notice. Keys are never saved.}
\item{review}{Creation-time list with allow_external=TRUE/FALSE. Omit transfer_consent for strict approval of each external payload. To confirm one creation-time scope, add transfer_consent=list(mode='project', confirmed=TRUE, reviewer='...', reason='...', categories=c('study_context','aggregate_qc','aggregate_markers','aggregate_design','aggregate_expression')). This binds the provider, prompt version and aggregate categories. Only requests within these categories skip repeated transfer approval. Payload previews remain available; no scientific approval is granted.}
\item{python}{Existing Python 3.9+ executable, detected by default.}
\item{browse}{Open the URL in the browser; FALSE returns it without browser dispatch.}
\item{reuse_processed}{Explicitly reuse processed layers and clusters. FALSE by default.}
\item{processed_reason}{Required rationale for processed reuse.}
\item{cluster_column}{Saved cluster column for processed reuse.}
}
\value{Invisibly, the service URL, PID, project ID and reuse status.}
\description{Thin R entry into the existing local launcher and review service. Returns control to R. New projects start at strategy review; explicit processed reuse starts at annotation. Neither startup nor reopening approves labels or starts analysis/provider requests. The service allows bound review writes and explicit local continuation. Existing project authority is never replaced.}
\details{Existing projects must match project format version 3 in the format marker and authoritative state. The format gate runs before project writes or write locks; a missing, damaged or mismatched format is rejected. Use the original software environment or create a new project. The workbench may start a read-only R preflight, which performs no scientific analysis or model request. Requires the installed R package and Python 3.9+. Browser assets and Python modules ship with the package; the Python interpreter is not included. Runtime asset hashes and R function signatures must match. No software or credentials are installed. The current R executable and library paths are passed to the existing launcher. Repeating the call with the same project reuses its matching live service, or restarts a stopped service. Use sc_start(project_dir="analysis") to reopen from protected checkpoints and saved settings. No input is rebound; a changed file at the original recorded path is still rejected. When input is explicitly supplied, original RDS path/checksum and saved configuration must match. For 10x, the exact source receipt and generated input checksum must match; temporary adapter paths may differ. Source inputs and import options must be unchanged. The protected input checkpoint retains source provenance. Generated transport RDS files are removed after startup. Use \code{sc_run_open()} for a read-only result viewer.}
